=base:main-content.cmark

# Changelog: tramaj-halogen

Release history of `tramaj-halogen`, the Halogen host: folds an evaluated Node into Halogen.HTML. Releases happen when there are
major changes rather than on a schedule; each entry below is one version.
Every implementation has its own page like this one, and each page is
tagged so the site builds one Atom feed per implementation:
#changelog #purescript #tramaj-halogen

The unreleased entry has breaking changes to numbers:
[Migrating to integers and floats](/migrating-to-integers-and-floats.html)
says what to do about each.

=base:main-content.tramaj-doc
@version=import("changelog/version", {"package": "tramaj-halogen"})
.div(class: "changelog",
  $version({
      "version": "(none)",
      "date": "unreleased",
      "summary": "Consumed as a git dependency; no registry release yet.",
      "changes": [
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "\`Tramaj.Halogen.foldToHalogen\`, wiring each \`action(...)\` to the host's own Action type."
          },
          {
              "kind": "changed",
              "text": "Breaking: a scalar is rendered by its type, as \`str\` writes it: an integer as its digits, a float always with a fraction or an exponent. The float \`1.0\` renders as \`1.0\` where it rendered as \`1\`."
          },
          {
              "kind": "changed",
              "text": "Breaking: takes \`Tramaj.Json\` values where it took Argonaut's, following \`tramaj-purs\`."
          },
          {
              "kind": "fixed",
              "text": "An integer beyond 32 bits is no longer rendered with a fraction."
          },
          {
              "kind": "added",
              "text": "A term renders as the call that built it, such as \`sum(#0, 1)\`, in a \`code\` element in text position, like a symbol."
          }
      ]
  }).rendered)

